[2.233026, "o", "Initialized mnema project at ~/your-repository/.mnema\r\n"]
[2.233284, "o", "  identity: mnid:3114c1e99c941056ca60d3c74dacfbb5438103d0ce8c0d51bfb0d4dde3bbc4b6\r\n"]
[2.233406, "o", "  backup key: created and enrolled, private half at ~/.mnema/identity/backup/92f87ffb9cd6583a51bb022eb37e48309776c23f1a5475973529c61d0df1b508.key\r\n  Move that file off this machine: a backup left on this disk is lost with it.\r\n"]
[2.23472, "o", "  Created AGENTS.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\n  Created .claude/rules/mnema-instructions.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\n"]
[2.234807, "o", "  Created .github/instructions/mnema-instructions.instructions.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\n  Created .cursor/rules/mnema-instructions.mdc, with the mnema instructions.\r\n"]
[2.23488, "o", "  Each holds the mnema instructions an agent host reads at the start of a session: when to\r\n"]
[2.234975, "o", "  call the mnema tools, and what never goes in the record. `mnema instructions --remove`\r\n"]
[2.235032, "o", "  takes them out.\r\n\r\n  mnema writes no other file of yours. In Claude Code the mnema plugin hands this record to\r\n  each session on its own. Without it, `mnema brief > MNEMA.md` puts what governs this\r\n"]
[2.235101, "o", "  project in a file of its own (the `>` replaces the whole of the file it names), and\r\n  one line in a `CLAUDE.md` brings that file in (an `AGENTS.md` is read there only\r\n  where no `CLAUDE.md` exists):\r\n    @MNEMA.md\r\n"]
[2.23526, "o", "\r\n"]
[2.23532, "o", "  Commit `.mnema/` with the repository: the record travels with it, and every clone reads it.\r\n"]
[2.23538, "o", "  Off until switched on: edit-first-write-gate, user-corrections.\r\n  Turn one on with `mnema switch on <name>`; `mnema switch` lists every channel.\r\n  Next: `mnema decision record <title> <rationale>`; `mnema status` shows where things stand.\r\n"]
[3.849965, "o", "\u001b[2m# write down a call, with the reasoning and what was turned down\u001b[0m\r\n"]
